{
  "decision": "map_front",
  "rationale": "Round 3 of 4, 300/400 evals used, so this is the last exploration round and the reserved front-mapping budget should be spent now. Evidence: (1) the feasible front is 100% `pipelined` (104/140 feasible; iterative, unrolled_k and pipelined_m are 0/10, 0/15, 0/135 feasible), so the front lives in exactly one family and its full ranges can be mapped directly. (2) The front is not covering the objective ranges: area spans 41539..80076 against an HV reference of 100000 (a ~20k um^2 gap that can still add hypervolume), and accuracy spans 12..18.7 bits while the pipelined family has already demonstrated 23.75 bits, so the high-accuracy end of the trade-off is unmapped. (3) The min-area corner is fragile for the selection rule: the cheapest design (41539 um^2) sits at max_abs_err=0.000241 vs the 0.000244141 limit (only 0.02 bits of margin), and the spec warns that cheapest designs which only just pass the L1 sys_p99_batch_us bound (best seen 0.245 us vs 0.5 us) can be lost at L2 re-selection. A seeded NSGA-II sweep over the full pipelined ranges (data_width 8..28, n_iter 4..30, angle_guard -2..4, frac_guard 0..4, rounding trunc|round) both fills the area/accuracy gaps for hypervolume and densifies the cheap end of the front so L2 re-selection has robust alternatives to the marginal 41539 um^2 point. No next_plan needed for map_front."
  ,"next_plan": null
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Final round (4/4) and full budget (400/400 evals) are exhausted, so only stop/infeasible apply. Infeasible is ruled out: 145 of 400 evaluations are feasible and the front has 28 designs, with every constraint demonstrably reachable — throughput best seen 190 MSPS (>=32), max_abs_err best 7.07e-08 (<=2^-12), sys_p99_batch_us best 0.245 (<=0.5). The selection rule (min area_um2) is satisfiable on the front by pipelined [data_width=19 n_iter=14 angle_guard=-2 frac_guard=1 rounding=round] at area_um2=41539, accuracy_bits=12.02 (max_abs_err=2.41e-04, just inside the 2^-12 bound), throughput 132 MSPS. The front spans area 41539..80076 um2 and accuracy 12..18.7 bits, i.e. it already covers the useful trade-off region against the HV reference (100000, 12), and this round's hypervolume gain was only +0.6%, indicating diminishing returns. All four families were explored; iterative, unrolled_k and pipelined_m produced zero feasible designs (their throughput ceilings of 11, 8.4 and 91 MSPS respectively cannot service the 32-request burst within 0.5 us), so no unexplored family remains to add. Stopping is therefore the correct terminal action."
}
